messages:
alicia.k: ProspectX POC just hit another streaming failure during demo. Client crashed parsing stream (React WebView).\nben.s: What error did they see in console?\ndana_support: `Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input` from their parse call. Session id px-poc-431.
sse-bot: [sse-session-start] id=px-poc-431 model=redwood-3-small region=us-west-2
ryan_ps: Can you paste the raw server SSE lines?
dana_support: Server emitted: `data: {\"id\":1,\"t\":\"Part1\"}\ndata: {\"id\":1,\"t\":\"Part2\"}` connection closed before `\n\n` terminator for event 1. Proxy logs show `upstream_write_timeout` around same time.
mike_oncall: Looks like client/proxy closed mid-event. Client parser assumed each `data:` line is a full JSON object; that fails when logical objects span multiple `data:` frames.
enalicia.k: ProspectX is nervous and asked if this is our throttling. They saw a 429 earlier in another test.
dana_support: Confirmed no 429 on this session. Separate load test caused 429s earlier but unrelated.\bens.s: Immediate mitigations: 1) send them a tiny tolerant parser for WebView that accumulates until `\n\n` and then JSON.parse; 2) ask to test on direct connection (no corp proxy) to rule out proxy closes; 3) we can roll a canary server change to flush after each logical event for demo tokens.
ryan_ps: I'll accept the parser snippet to include in the POC docs.
dana_support: DMing snippet now. Snippet: ```js
// accumulate SSE data lines until blank line, then parse
let buf = '';
eventSource.onmessage = e => {
  buf += e.data;
  if (buf.includes('\n\n')) {
    const evts = buf.split('\n\n');
    for (let i=0;i<evts.length-1;i++){
      const payload = evts[i].split('\n').map(l=>l.replace(/^data:\s*/,'')).join('');
      try { handle(JSON.parse(payload)); } catch(e){ console.warn('partial-json',e); }
    }
    buf = evts[evts.length-1];
  }
};
```
mike_oncall: I'll also open infra ticket to bump proxy write timeout for demo window and enable a quick canary that forces flush after each SSE event for demo tokens.
alicia.k: Please share timeline; customer wants another demo tomorrow afternoon.
dana_support: Snippet sent and asked for HAR + client logs; infra ticket created.
ben.s: Add a short FAQ blurb to sales POC pack: "If embedding in WebView, use streaming-aware reassembly + keepalives."
alicia.k: Thanks everyone — will coordinate the next demo once canary is live. :thumbsup:
